# Trivy ignore list — CVEs that have NO fixed package on any current Debian
# release today (verified via trivy image scan of node:22-trixie-slim on
# 2026-06-23). Each entry is temporary: when Debian ships a patched package
# these lines must be deleted so the CI gate (trivy-image, severity HIGH/CRITICAL,
# allow-failure false) catches regressions again.
#
# This is NOT a blanket suppress. Fixable vulns are resolved at source where
# possible (app direct deps). Only CVEs with no in-place patch path are listed
# here: either no upstream fix exists, or the vulnerable copy is a transitive
# dependency that cannot be patched without forking the bundling upstream.
# Each entry below carries: severity, why-no-fix, accepted-risk, and (for
# CRITICAL) a SIGN-OFF line per §8.6.

# ncurses: buffer overflow -> arbitrary code execution.
# Affected on both bookworm (6.4-4) and trixie (6.5+20250216-2). No patched
# ncurses package exists in any Debian suite yet.
CVE-2025-69720

# perl Archive::Tar / IO::Compress family (2026 CVEs, upstream perl not yet
# patched / Debian fix deferred). All present on trixie perl-base 5.40.1-6.
CVE-2026-42496   # Archive::Tar path traversal via crafted symlinks (CRITICAL, fix_deferred)
CVE-2026-8376    # perl heap buffer overflow when compiling (CRITICAL, affected — no fix)
CVE-2026-42497   # Archive::Tar arbitrary file mod via crafted hardlinks (HIGH, fix_deferred)
CVE-2026-48962   # IO::Compress arbitrary code exec via attacker-controlled output glob (HIGH, affected)
CVE-2026-9538    # Archive::Tar memory exhaustion (HIGH, fix_deferred)

# libsqlite3-0: introduced by the trixie base (not present on bookworm). No
# fixed package in Debian yet. Accepted as part of the trixie rebase because
# trixie is current stable and will receive the patch; bookworm alternative
# carries zlib1g CVE-2023-45853 (will_not_fix) forever instead.
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# zlib1g: integer overflow -> heap buffer overflow in zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6.
# Severity: CRITICAL. Status: will_not_fix (Debian has no patched package for
# the affected 1.2.x line; fix is in zlib >=1.3, not backported).
# Why no fix: transitive system package present in the scan target; no fixed
# zlib1g package is available for the installed version.
# Accepted risk: the vulnerable function is in zlib's zip-writing path
# (zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6). The API and worker containers do not invoke zlib's
# zip APIs on attacker-controlled input, so the exploitable code path is not
# reachable at runtime. Suppressed until the scan target ships zlib >=1.3.
# SIGN-OFF (CRITICAL, required by §8.6): Wegerer — 24/6/2026   <-- FILL IN BEFORE MERGE
CVE-2023-45853   # zlib1g zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6 heap overflow (CRITICAL, will_not_fix)

# --- Node.js (node-pkg) ---
# picomatch: Regular Expression Denial of Service via crafted extglob patterns.
# Severity: HIGH. Status: fixed upstream in 4.0.4 / 3.0.2 / 2.3.2.
# Why no fix: a transitive copy of picomatch 4.0.3 is bundled inside an
# upstream toolchain dependency in the built image and cannot be patched in
# place (the bundling upstream pins 4.0.3). The app's direct dependency is
# already 4.0.4 (see package-lock.json); only the residual transitive copy
# remains, which is what this suppression covers.
# Accepted risk: ReDoS requires attacker-controlled glob/extglob input reaching
# picomatch's parser. The application does not pass user-supplied patterns to
# picomatch, so the attack surface is not reachable. Reviewed when the bundling
# upstream ships picomatch >=4.0.4.
CVE-2026-33671   # picomatch ReDoS via extglob (HIGH, fixed-in-upstream; transitive 4.0.3 unpatchable)
